  "body": "Replaces #466 by @mkinney (their commits kept as authored) with main merged in - the fork refuses maintainer pushes.\n\nResolution: the only conflict was the binary snapshot `crates/ui/tests/snapshots/egui_tool_editor.png`. `state.rs` auto-merged. Main's PNG was taken as a placeholder, and the snapshot was then regenerated on the merged tree. Only the tool-library controls this PR adds differ: the **Export library…** / **Import library…** buttons under Edit/Delete/New tool…, which push the Catalog list down by one row. The toolbar badge still reads `v0.0.0`. `egui_shell` snapshots did not change.\n\nTargeted gate (merged tree, debug):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_library`: 12 passed\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- tool_library tool_editor_snapshot egui_shell_snapshot` (CWD crates/ui, no UPDATE): 4 passed (`no_tool_routes_to_the_tool_library`, `tool_editor_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n\nChangelog: The Tool library page exports the document's tools to a `.camtools` file and imports one back (one undo step; names already in the document are never overwritten, and a bad file is refused by tool name)\n\nRefs #300\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
